    "problem_statement": "### URL Shortening Issue in InvalidCredentialError\n\nHello!\n\nI've encountered an issue with the `InvalidCredentialError` in the `safety` package. It seems that the URL provided in the error message for invalid credentials has been changed to a shortened link, which is causing some unexpected behavior.\n\n**Steps to Reproduce:**\n\n1. Trigger an `InvalidCredentialError` by using an invalid API key with the `safety` CLI tool.\n2. Observe the error message that is generated.\n\n**Expected Result:**\n\nThe error message should contain a direct link to the documentation page for invalid API key errors, which is `https://docs.safetycli.com/safety-docs/support/invalid-api-key-error`.\n\n**Actual Result:**\n\nThe error message contains a shortened URL (`https://bit.ly/3OY2wEI`) instead of the full documentation link. This change might lead to confusion or issues with accessing the correct documentation page.\n\nThis change in the URL format seems unnecessary and could potentially lead to issues if the shortened URL service experiences downtime or if the link is altered. It would be preferable to revert to using the full URL to ensure reliability and transparency.\n\nThanks for looking into this!"
  }
